# Notes Management & Review REST API

A production-oriented **RESTful Notes Management API** built with **Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB, and Mongoose**. The application provides secure user authentication, personal and public note management, note reviews, and search functionality through a clean and scalable backend architecture.

## Key Features

* **User Authentication & Authorization**

  * User registration and login
  * JWT-based authentication
  * Protected API endpoints
  * User-specific resource ownership

* **Notes Management**

  * Create, read, update, and delete notes
  * Private and public note visibility
  * Retrieve authenticated user's notes
  * Retrieve publicly available notes
  * Search public notes by title or content
  * Notes sorted by creation date

* **Review System**

  * Add reviews to notes
  * Retrieve reviews associated with a note
  * Update and delete reviews
  * User-based review ownership

* **Data Relationships**

  * User → Notes relationship
  * User → Reviews relationship
  * Note → Reviews relationship
  * MongoDB references with Mongoose `populate()`

* **API Design**

  * RESTful endpoint architecture
  * Structured JSON responses
  * HTTP status code handling
  * Centralized controller-based architecture
  * Middleware-based authentication and authorization

## Technology Stack

**Backend:** Node.js, Express.js
**Database:** MongoDB, Mongoose
**Authentication:** JWT, bcrypt
**API Testing:** Postman
**Architecture:** REST API, MVC-style structure

## Example API Endpoints

```text
POST   /api/users/register
POST   /api/users/login

POST   /api/notes
GET    /api/notes
GET    /api/notes/public
GET    /api/notes/search?search=node
GET    /api/notes/:id
PUT    /api/notes/:id
DELETE /api/notes/:id

POST   /api/reviews/:noteId
GET    /api/reviews/:noteId
PUT    /api/reviews/:id
DELETE /api/reviews/:id
```

## Project Highlights

Designed with a focus on **security, maintainability, scalability, and clean API architecture**, while implementing real-world backend concepts such as authentication, authorization, database relationships, CRUD operations, resource ownership, search, reviews, and protected routes.
